==Battleground==
*5 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*5 [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 8 seconds<sup>240f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gabriel]]s spawn after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>, delay 8~13.33 seconds<sup>240f~400f</sup>.
*1 [[Loincloth Cat (Enemy)|Loincloth Cat]] spawns after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Loincloth Cat (Enemy)|Loincloth Cat]] spawns after 120 seconds<sup>3,600f</sup>.
*1 [[Loincloth Cat (Enemy)|Loincloth Cat]] spawns after 186.67 seconds<sup>5,600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 90% HP:
**1 [[Loincloth Cat (Enemy)|Loincloth Cat]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 80% HP:
**1 [[Loincloth Cat (Enemy)|Loincloth Cat]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 70% HP:
**2 [[Loincloth Cat (Enemy)|Loincloth Cats]] spawn, delay 2 seconds<sup>60f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Cats with high range or a large enough effective [[Long Distance]] range are very useful for helping defeat the Loincloth Cats. Cats with level 4 or more [[Wave Attack|Wave Attacks]] and/or [[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|Rusher-class units]] are also extremely important, given you time them properly.

If you don't own any cats with [[Long Distance|LD]] or [[Wave Attack|Wave Attacks]] try using [[:Category:Tanker-class Cats|Tankers]] like [[Mythical Titan Cat]] or [[Wrestling Cat]] to chip down the Loincloths slowly, be careful of the high damage peons though, since they could easily shred them if your tanks aren't bulky enough.

